  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "What to Ask Before Starting a Rental Property Repair",
    "text": "What to Ask Before Starting a Rental Property Repair",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "When you're dealing with rental property repairs, it's not just about fixing what's broken right now; it's also about thinking ahead. Before you even get a quote, consider these questions: Is this repair a quick fix, or is it part of a larger issue that might be better addressed during a unit turnover or capital project? What systems are critical for safety and habitability, and which ones are likely to fail soon? Prioritizing safety-critical systems like plumbing or electrical is always the smart move. When talking to contractors, make sure they provide a written scope of work, an itemized estimate, and proof of liability insurance. You also want to understand their process for unexpected issues. Responsiveness and the ability to coordinate different trades efficiently are key for rental properties, as vacancies can be costly. And remember, for any electrical, plumbing, or structural work, it's best to use licensed professionals to avoid future headaches or code compliance problems.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
